WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
Good morning, Hank, it's Wednesday. I must defy the Wadsworth constant!

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.940
The Wadsworth constant holds that the first 30% of a YouTube video is always skippable.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:12.460
Most pumpkins are sold by the pound, so pro tip: bring a screwdriver and a straw to the pumpkin farm;

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.860
stick the screwdriver in there, pop in your straw,

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.360
suck out some pumpkin juice, and bam! Cheaper pumpkin!

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.760
Don't tell me pumpkin juice doesn't exist, Muggles!

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.100
If you want to seem like you've read James Joyce's Ulysses without actually reading it,

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.920
just memorize these three quotations:

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.260
"'History,' Stephen said, 'is a nightmare from which I am trying to awake.'",

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.820
"Love loves to love love," and finally,

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:39.740
arguably the first eight words of post-modernism, "O Jamesy, let me up out of this."

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.700
Pro tip: insert 'arguably' into a sentence, and it becomes true!

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.020
How do you like them apples, Wadsworth? How's that for an entertaining and informative first 30%?

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:51.420
Right, so, Hank, two important things have happened: first, I have now signed my name over 100,000 times

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.100
in my mission to sign every copy of the first printing of The Fault In Our Stars.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.220
Some people think that I'm cheating or using a stamp or that the books won't actually be signed,

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:01.000
but you're about to see me sign some. I AM NOT A CHEAT!

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.220
Two: Hank! Hank! Hank! Do you know Laurena Segura, Nerd Factor winner for her amazing song 'Permafrost'?

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:10.120
Well, she has an EP that is out on iTunes through DFTBA Records by popular demand!

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.120
Look how popular the demand was!

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.560
It includes not only 'Permafrost', but a song in French and this song, 'Fireflies of Montreal'.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.600
[Laurena singing] Ripple in the midnight clouds

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.000
No stars at the horizon

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:35.680
Flicker from an old streetlight

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.480
Attracts the moths who claim the night

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:47.560
Satellites that pass overhead

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:52.360
In the ribcage sky

00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:00.560
If they stop, we're good as dead

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.040
So then what good am I?

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.220
But I've heard from encounters with the past

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:18.700
That creatures gentle glowing never last

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.180
Oh, won't someone tell me after all

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:28.820
What happened to the fireflies of Montreal?

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:39.680
Darkness in the alleyways

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:44.480
At least for some

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:51.560
In the sixties flew away

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.360
Left a few, now there are none

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:03.140
But I've heard from encounters with the past

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:09.200
Gentle creatures glowing never last

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:15.340
Won't someone tell me after all

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:19.560
What happened to the fireflies of Montreal?

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:27.120
Won't someone tell me after all

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:32.340
What happened to the fireflies of Montreal?

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:37.540
Hank, I don't want to hurt your feeling or anything, but Laurena is fast replacing you as my third favorite band.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:41.480
iTunes link in the dooblydoo. Hank, you're still my favorite video blogger if that makes you feel better,

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:47.760
your video on Wednesday was brilliant, I can't wait to see- it was on Monday. Gah! I'm so bad at days!

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.940
Alright, I'm gonna go back to signing, but I will see you on Friday. That was too much of a gesticulation, that

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:56.840
was like waaahhaaghgh! Maybe I'll just leave that in.

